Track 3: Skarn Play
- Story & Context: The stone, now known locally as the "Whispering Skarn," became an unsettling pilgrimage site in the desolate outskirts, drawing curious wanderers who swore they could feel a profound chill radiating from its smooth, black surface, even on warm days. People began to speak of strange, non-euclidean geometries appearing in the frost on window panes and the bizarre, echoing melodies carried on the wind, a phenomenon some attributed to the accelerated, groaning melt of the great ice sheets further north. Elara, having retreated from the burgeoning cult around her discovery, was last seen tracing faint, iridescent patterns in the condensing mist on the old dock walls, muttering, "We built our cities on a lie, a slow decay," a haunting lament for the world slowly succumbing to the glacial cadence.
